      "deletions": 1,
      "filename": "docs/source/advanced/custom_dataset_factories.md",
      "patch": "@@ -94,7 +94,7 @@ data. A new primary format normally needs:\n 3. a factory derived from the narrowest suitable base, usually\n    `BaseSingleFileDatasetFactory` or `BaseManifestShardListDatasetFactory`;\n 4. format-specific `_build_reader` and `load_sample` implementations;\n-5. `as_file_store()` only if key lookup, joins, mounts, or primary auxiliary\n+5. `as_file_store()` only if key lookup, mounts, or primary auxiliary\n    access are supported;\n 6. a stable, serializable `config()` used for diagnostics;\n 7. preparation or index-generation code when ordinal access cannot be derived",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-Energon/raw/ab76ea640f9a973dc88b4fa1888f6154ed2a5d53/docs%2Fsource%2Fadvanced%2Fcustom_dataset_factories.md",
      "sha": "26842cc1a71305856517e44bf1a5440afb1b296a",
      "status": "modified"
    },
    {
      "additions": 2,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-Energon/blob/ab76ea640f9a973dc88b4fa1888f6154ed2a5d53/docs%2Fsource%2Finternals%2Fcode_structure.md",
      "changes": 4,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/Megatron-Energon/contents/docs%2Fsource%2Finternals%2Fcode_structure.md?ref=ab76ea640f9a973dc88b4fa1888f6154ed2a5d53",
      "deletions": 2,
      "filename": "docs/source/internals/code_structure.md",
      "patch": "@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@ The implementation lives under `src/megatron/energon`. Its main layers are:\n \n | Package | Responsibility |\n | --- | --- |\n-| `recipe` | Parse and resolve recipe graphs, references, blends, joins, subsets, and split overrides. |\n+| `recipe` | Parse and resolve recipe graphs, references, blends, subsets, and split overrides. |\n | `flavors` | Detect prepared dataset formats and construct their readers and runtime datasets. |\n | `wrappers` | Compose iteration behavior such as mapping, batching, blending, packing, and epochizing. |\n | `task_encoder` | Build the user-facing loading pipeline and invoke application-specific encoding hooks. |\n@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@ Energon has two distinct random-access interfaces. They should not be conflated:\n 1. **Ordinal iteration** uses an `IndexedSampleReader`. `reader[index]` accepts an integer sample ordinal\n    and returns a `SampleRecord`. A `DatasetSampler` maps the worker's iteration order to those ordinals.\n 2. **Key and part lookup** uses `FileStore`, `SamplePartReader`, and related readers. These interfaces\n-   locate a sample or auxiliary part by a string key and are used by crude datasets, joins, mounts, and\n+   locate a sample or auxiliary part by a string key and are used by crude datasets, mounts, and\n    restore-by-key paths.\n \n A format can support ordinary indexed training without exposing all file-store capabilities. Conversely,",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-Energon/raw/ab76ea640f9a973dc88b4fa1888f6154ed2a5d53/docs%2Fsource%2Finternals%2Fcode_structure.md",
      "sha": "7e78bdebedd96bc25a182c014680ea8cabc45cf9",
      "status": "modified"
    },
    {
      "additions": 2,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-Energon/blob/ab76ea640f9a973dc88b4fa1888f6154ed2a5d53/docs%2Fsource%2Finternals%2Fdataset_formats.md",
      "changes": 4,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/Megatron-Energon/contents/docs%2Fsource%2Finternals%2Fdataset_formats.md?ref=ab76ea640f9a973dc88b4fa1888f6154ed2a5d53",
      "deletions": 2,
      "filename": "docs/source/internals/dataset_formats.md",
      "patch": "@@ -59,7 +59,7 @@ Do not use string keys on `IndexedSampleReader`; string lookup belongs to `FileS\n \n `FileStore` retrieves `(data, SourceInfo)` for a string key and reports the underlying path. Part-aware\n readers extend that model to enumerate or retrieve named parts. These interfaces support auxiliary media,\n-joins, mounts, and crude-dataset access.\n+mounts, and crude-dataset access.\n \n When adding file-store support:\n \n@@ -96,7 +96,7 @@ Use this checklist:\n 3. **Reader:** implement integer ordinal access, length, resource cleanup, and `SampleRecord` provenance.\n 4. **Factory:** subclass the appropriate indexed base and implement only the format-specific hooks.\n 5. **Filtering:** verify `part_filter` and exclusions.\n-6. **Key access:** implement `FileStore` or part readers if joins, mounts, or auxiliary lookup require it.\n+6. **Key access:** implement `FileStore` or part readers if mounts or auxiliary lookup require it.\n 7. **Detection:** register a provider at the least surprising priority and test competing path shapes.\n 8. **Configuration:** ensure `config()` contains stable leaf identity fields used by diagnostics.\n 9. **Exports and docs:** expose the supported API and document preparation and recipe syntax.",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-Energon/raw/ab76ea640f9a973dc88b4fa1888f6154ed2a5d53/docs%2Fsource%2Finternals%2Fdataset_formats.md",
      "sha": "840fcecaeb412b99ca440e5db8eedfef028b848a",
      "status": "modified"
    },
